message: "If you use CausalLoss-Fin, please cite it as below."
title: "CausalLoss-Fin: Attributing Financial-Agent Loss to Decisions and Infrastructure Faults"
abstract: "A causal layer over the FinalityBench benchmark that intervenes on both an agent's decisions and on individual infrastructure faults - dropped, delayed, duplicated and reordered messages - and splits a policy's monetary loss exactly three ways into an infrastructure effect, a policy differential against the best implementable policy, and a reference-policy residual. Two of the three can be negative, so none is a share; Shapley allocation then divides the infrastructure effect across individual messages; those allocations are signed and satisfy efficiency, summing to the effect, and a message whose repair would have increased the loss carries a negative one. Includes a decomposition of a realised fault schedule into individually repairable instances, Shapley allocation across messages, minimal sufficient causes, and a planted-ground-truth suite in four strata including the overdetermined case."
